From f822c1e9dfb4534425e6c9fbc3c951fe11173d30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exploitizm <351399878+exploitizm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:35:17 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: mesh shaders run as compute are cached with their
 pipelines

Their pipelines were compiled at every launch (about two minutes for Ocarina
of Time before its first frame): the compute pass and the copy vertex shader
named the device's buffers by address, so neither could be cached.

The addresses now come at the draw, in a block uploaded per draw
(radv_mesh_compute_block: the task emulation's records and payload ring,
the buffer's header and slots) that both shaders take as their
gs_compute_draw argument, as a geometry shader's passes and rasterization
copy do (RADV_GS_COMPUTE_MESH for the compute pass, RADV_GS_COMPUTE_RAST for
the copy). The pipeline cache keeps the compute pass after the pipeline's
other shaders, with its vertices a workgroup and capacity in the object's
data. Whether the path is on is part of the cache's UUID.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
